Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?agent=20wallet:=20one=20capability=20per=20send?=
 =?UTF-8?q?er=20(=E2=91=A2=20patch=200008,=20=E2=91=A3=20AUTH-ROUTES=20A1)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

issue-capability {source: mcp|ai} issues a token bound to one sender and
replaces only that sender's previous token; revoke-capability {source}
withdraws one. The unscoped token (create / rotate-capability) is
unchanged, so existing clients keep working. A sender's token acts as
that sender only (BadCapability otherwise). whoami names the bound
source; the public view lists senders and versions, never a hash.
Key-free test (fake keyring, fixed owner constant, whoami).
